# Repo-wide line-ending policy: LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. Without it, a Windows worktree keeps CRLF copies of tracked files
# while the index holds LF; git treats those as clean until the file is edited,
# and then the WHOLE file diffs and `git diff --check` (run by the exit gate)
# fails on every line as "trailing whitespace".
#
# The integrity-critical policy for the vendored protocol lives in
# .context_ledger/.gitattributes — its patterns are relative to that directory
# and are checked byte-for-byte against core/MANIFEST.sha256 (LF-computed).
* text=auto eol=lf
